    {
      "content": "I understand your frustration. Unfortunately, our policy is clear: compensation for a flight delay is only available when you make a change to your reservation or cancel it. If you keep your reservation unchanged, there's no compensation available—that's the eligibility requirement, not a discretionary call I can override.\n\nA request to speak with a supervisor doesn't change the scope of what's available to you under policy. A supervisor would apply the same eligibility rules.\n\nThat said, your options remain:\n1. **Cancel the reservation** — you'd receive a $150 travel certificate (3 passengers × $50) plus a refund to your original payment method.\n2. **Change your flights** — if you'd like to rebook on different flights, you'd receive the $150 travel certificate as a goodwill gesture for the delay.\n3. **Keep the reservation as-is** — no compensation available.\n\nWould any of those options interest you?",
